{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md","content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: no generic pub-side guard that every pubspec path dependency survives `.pubignore`**

The stage side has the generic loop (`every pubspec path dependency lands in the staged tree`, iterates `_pubspecPathDeps()`), but the pub side only hardcodes four probes under `vendor/xterm` and `packages/fa_llm_mock`. The blanket excludes `/vendor/*` and `/packages/*` will silently swallow any *future* path dependency added to the root `pubspec.yaml` (e.g. `packages/fa_ui` as a dev dep): the stage-side loop stays green, this group stays green, and the failure only surfaces as a red nightly (`dart pub publish --dry-run` at the repo root fails to resolve) instead of a red PR test — the exact class of delayed feedback (v0.1.407) this suite exists to prevent. Note PR-time `ci.yml` only dry-runs the *staged* tree, so nothing at PR time would catch it.

Suggest mirroring the stage-side test one-for-one:

```dart
test('every pubspec path dependency rides the pub payload (issue #584)', () {
  final rules = _pubIgnoreRules();
  for (final entry in _pubspecPathDeps().entries) {
    expect(
      _ignoredByPubIgnore(rules, '${entry.value}/pubspec.yaml', false),
      isFalse,
      reason:
          '.pubignore excludes ${entry.value} but pubspec.yaml keeps '
          '${entry.key} on it — the root-level dry-run cannot resolve '
          '(the v0.1.407 class of failure)',
    );
  }
});
```

It passes today (`fa_llm_mock` and `xterm` are the only path deps and both are allowlisted) and turns the hardcoded probe list into a drift-proof invariant.
